# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=development

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORS
# Comma-separated list of allowed browser origins. No trailing slash, no path.
# "*" is rejected. REQUIRED when NODE_ENV=production - the server refuses to
# start without it, so production can never run a permissive CORS policy.
# Left empty in development, localhost dev origins are allowed automatically.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Limits
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
BODY_LIMIT=1mb
RATE_LIMIT_MAX=300
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MINUTES=15

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (JWT)
#
# JWT_SECRET signs access tokens (HS256). It is SENSITIVE - never commit a
# real value, never share it in chat or email, and use a different secret per
# environment. Minimum 32 characters; placeholder values are rejected.
#
# REQUIRED when NODE_ENV=production - the server refuses to start without it.
# Left unset in development, a random per-process secret is generated and a
# warning is logged (tokens then stop working after a restart).
#
# Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
JWT_SECRET=

# Non-secret token labels, validated on every verification.
JWT_ISSUER=nexelvoria-academy
JWT_AUDIENCE=nexelvoria-academy-api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Microsoft SQL Server 2025
#
# NOW READ BY THE APPLICATION. `src/config/sqlserver.ts` parses these and
# `src/db/sqlserver.pool.ts` opens one shared connection pool from them.
# Verify with `npm run db:check`, which runs SELECT 1 and prints no password.
#
# The FOUR identity values below are required; the rest have working
# defaults. Whitespace counts as missing, so a blank placeholder cannot be
# mistaken for a real setting.
#
# Nothing below is a real value. Nothing below may EVER be committed with a
# real value: `.gitignore` excludes `.env` and `.env.*` apart from this
# template and `.env.test`.
#
# Access method is still unconfirmed (handoff Q-C1: direct `mssql` driver,
# stored-procedures-only, or a data service in front). These names assume the
# driver; a procedures-only mandate would not change them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Hostname or `host\instance`. No port here - use SQLSERVER_PORT.
SQLSERVER_HOST=

# Default 1433. Integer.
SQLSERVER_PORT=1433

# Database name. The backend connects to ONE database.
SQLSERVER_DATABASE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (handoff Q-C3)
#
# Three options, and the preference is the third:
#
#   1. SQL authentication      - set SQLSERVER_USER and SQLSERVER_PASSWORD
#   2. Windows / AD integrated - set neither; the host identity is used
#   3. Entra ID managed identity - set neither; PREFERRED, because it means
#      there is no stored password anywhere, and SQLSERVER_PASSWORD below
#      stops existing as a concern
#
# SQLSERVER_PASSWORD is THE ONLY SECRET in this list. Deliver it through the
# agreed secret store - never by email, chat or a pull request.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SQLSERVER_USER=
SQLSERVER_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transport security (handoff Q-C7)
#
# SQLSERVER_ENCRYPT must be `true` in every shared environment, and the
# application will refuse to start with it false when NODE_ENV=production -
# the same fail-closed rule CORS_ORIGINS and JWT_SECRET already follow.
#
# SQLSERVER_TRUST_SERVER_CERT is a DEVELOPMENT-ONLY escape hatch for a
# self-signed certificate. It disables certificate verification, so it must
# never be true outside a developer's machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SQLSERVER_ENCRYPT=true
SQLSERVER_TRUST_SERVER_CERT=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connection pool (handoff Q-C4)
#
# Per APPLICATION INSTANCE, not per cluster. The database team needs to know
# how many instances are provisioned to size max connections; we need to know
# their ceiling to set this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SQLSERVER_POOL_MIN=0
SQLSERVER_POOL_MAX=10

# Milliseconds to wait for a connection from the pool before failing. A low
# value fails fast under load, which is preferable to queueing requests
# behind an exhausted pool until they time out at the client.
SQLSERVER_POOL_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# Milliseconds before an individual statement is cancelled. Guards against
# one pathological query holding a pooled connection indefinitely.
SQLSERVER_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development staff accounts (dev/ harness only)
#
# `npm run dev:integration` seeds one ACTIVE account per staff role so the
# Teacher, Admin and Super Admin portals can be signed into locally.
#
# Leave these UNSET and a fresh random password is generated per process and
# printed once to the terminal. Set one to keep a stable password across
# restarts - useful, but it must still satisfy the argon2 password policy
# (8+ chars, upper, lower, digit, symbol) or seeding fails loudly.
#
# These are LOCAL DEVELOPMENT values. `dev/` is excluded from the production
# build and refuses to load under NODE_ENV=production, and `.gitignore`
# excludes `.env`, so nothing here can ship. Never reuse a real password.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEV_SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# DEV_SEED_TEACHER_PASSWORD=
# DEV_SEED_SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Login lockout (decision D4)
# Consecutive failed logins that lock an account. Defaults to 5 when unset.
# Lockout is PERMANENT until cleared (Q4a): until password-reset or
# account-unlock APIs exist, recovery requires a controlled database
# intervention. Not a secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MAX_FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS=5
